<title>CANADA: United Grain board to study takeover offer.</title>
<headline>United Grain board to study takeover offer.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Grain Growers board of director will study a takeover offer made earlier Thursday by Alberta Wheat Pool and Manitoba Pool Elevators for all outstanding common shares at C$13.75 each, UGG's chief executive said.</p>
<p>&quot;The board will need time to assess the adequacy and terms of the offer and we will make a statement when they've had time to do that,&quot; UGG Chief Executive Officer Brian Hayward told Reuters.</p>
</text>
